WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.598
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:13.868 --> 00:14.702
FASTER

3
00:17.455 --> 00:18.289
MORE

4
00:20.875 --> 00:21.709
CHEAPER

5
00:26.131 --> 00:27.924
ACHIEVE 150% OF TARGET

6
00:43.898 --> 00:45.984
Time to eat, everyone!

7
00:46.067 --> 00:48.903
You need to finish more work first! Is that clear?

8
00:48.987 --> 00:51.906
If we don't meet our quota today, you're all working overtime!

9
01:02.208 --> 01:03.209
Yeon-joo.

10
01:04.961 --> 01:06.379
Just do it after you eat.

11
01:08.131 --> 01:09.757
Yeah, all right.

12
01:09.841 --> 01:11.176
KYUNGIL TEXTILE

13
01:11.259 --> 01:13.219
At least I have something good to eat.

14
01:13.303 --> 01:15.763
Enjoy your lunches.

15
01:17.682 --> 01:21.603
Hey, Yeon-joo. What is that? You worked as a maid before, didn't you?

16
01:21.686 --> 01:24.814
What kind of side dishes are those for a young lady to be eating?

17
01:25.481 --> 01:27.817
Where's the time to actually cook anything?

18
01:28.610 --> 01:30.695
Or the money to buy groceries?

19
01:32.197 --> 01:33.323
It tastes pretty good though.

20
01:33.406 --> 01:35.950
That's because you send all your salary home.

21
01:36.451 --> 01:40.413
Oh, Yeon-joo, you thrifty little thing. You're really going to do well in life.

22
01:40.496 --> 01:43.208
- Where'd you just come from? - You don't know about it?

23
01:44.000 --> 01:46.252
I heard something about our union president.

24
01:46.336 --> 01:48.504
- He sided with the company, not us. - What?

25
01:49.255 --> 01:50.590
Yeong-chun did that?

26
01:53.760 --> 01:56.095
- I knew that bastard looked shady. - But then…

27
01:57.263 --> 01:58.348
I mean,

28
01:59.390 --> 02:00.850
what about us?

29
02:02.101 --> 02:03.853
What's gonna happen to us now?

30
02:04.395 --> 02:05.647
Do we continue?

31
02:05.730 --> 02:07.023
Yeon-joo.

32
02:08.066 --> 02:10.610
We're not just machines. We can't work endlessly.

33
02:11.569 --> 02:14.155
They keep stomping us to death. We have to squirm a little at least.

34
02:15.448 --> 02:17.075
Because we're human beings.

35
02:20.828 --> 02:22.914
Hey!

36
02:22.997 --> 02:25.541
- Hey, they're coming! Run! - Come here!

37
02:25.625 --> 02:27.752
Come here! Shut your mouth!

38
02:27.835 --> 02:29.712
How dare some factory girls incite a riot?

39
02:31.005 --> 02:34.050
Come on. Get it!

40
02:35.677 --> 02:36.719
Let's go!

41
02:36.803 --> 02:38.346
Yeah, stay down!

42
02:39.681 --> 02:41.557
All of this off. You hear that?

43
02:42.058 --> 02:43.977
You're fired! Every last one of you!

44
02:44.060 --> 02:46.396
Come on, hurry up! Come on, let's go!

45
02:46.479 --> 02:47.855
UNIONS ARE NOT A CRIME

46
02:47.939 --> 02:49.816
What kind of nonsense is this?

47
03:47.832 --> 03:50.877
DEAD-END JOB

48
03:52.211 --> 03:55.089
NEO WORLD AFTER DARK

49
04:14.233 --> 04:15.485
What the hell?

50
04:19.947 --> 04:22.408
Uh, hey, whoa. Wh… What the fuck is happening?

51
04:22.492 --> 04:23.910
What are you doing here?

52
04:31.292 --> 04:35.213
I couldn't get in touch with that woman, and the owner here won't tell me anything.

53
04:35.296 --> 04:37.507
Hey, so, um, that's, uh… It's, um…

54
04:38.007 --> 04:39.509
W… Well, I'm sorry.

55
04:40.385 --> 04:42.637
You are seriously such a…

56
04:44.847 --> 04:47.767
It's okay. You're alive, so we're good. It's all okay, I just--

57
04:49.018 --> 04:49.852
Mm.

58
04:51.562 --> 04:52.480
Come in.

59
05:00.029 --> 05:05.952
That's 128,384,000 won.

60
05:08.079 --> 05:09.122
Here you go.

61
05:09.205 --> 05:10.665
One hundred…

62
05:12.166 --> 05:14.252
You're gonna need a bag for that much cash.

63
05:15.211 --> 05:16.754
The bag is complimentary.

64
05:39.193 --> 05:40.611
Come on. Let's go.

65
05:40.695 --> 05:42.530
See you both soon.

66
05:45.241 --> 05:47.493
- Hey, I have to ask-- - You better not give Hyeok-jun gigs.

67
05:47.577 --> 05:49.495
Am I clear?

68
05:50.746 --> 05:54.167
Well, the supply of jobs is only proportionate to the demand, isn't it?

69
05:55.293 --> 05:56.461
No demand, right?

70
05:57.670 --> 06:00.006
- Huh? - Tell me. Do you need these jobs or not?

71
06:01.632 --> 06:02.967
N… No, I'm all good.

72
06:03.050 --> 06:04.051
Hear that?

73
06:04.677 --> 06:06.220
Let's go. Come on.

74
06:10.433 --> 06:12.226
Holy shit! This is crazy.

75
06:12.310 --> 06:14.896
How much is this? We're not dreaming right now, are we?

76
06:15.396 --> 06:19.275
FIRE HOT TTEOKBOKKI

77
06:19.358 --> 06:21.777
- Cheers! Cheers, cheers. - Cheers!

78
06:21.861 --> 06:23.654
There's no better place to eat, right?

79
06:24.363 --> 06:26.115
A lot of this meat's for you, Mom. Have more.

80
06:26.199 --> 06:28.117
- Oh, no, no. - Hey, Ji-yoon, can you slow it down?

81
06:28.201 --> 06:30.286
Ugh, come on. Stop being so weird about food.

82
06:31.329 --> 06:34.123
Hey, now that you paid your debt off, do you feel a little more relaxed?

83
06:35.208 --> 06:37.460
Debt? That's news to me.

84
06:38.169 --> 06:39.253
What debt do you have?

85
06:39.337 --> 06:41.297
Oh, no, no, no, no. Nope, I paid it all off.

86
06:41.380 --> 06:43.382
Mom, he lost his money betting on stocks.

87
06:43.466 --> 06:47.887
On stocks? What money did you have to invest in the stock market? Huh?

88
06:48.554 --> 06:50.056
Well, uh, here's the thing…

89
06:51.474 --> 06:53.851
How could you be so reckless, you little punk?!

90
06:53.935 --> 06:55.853
Your apartment? Is the deposit gone?

91
06:55.937 --> 06:58.439
The deposit's still there! That money didn't get touched, I swear!

92
06:58.523 --> 07:01.609
- Is that true? Be honest with me! - Mom, he's honest. He's honest.

93
07:03.653 --> 07:05.029
Seriously, Mom, I promise.

94
07:05.112 --> 07:07.823
I put my life on the line, worked hard, and paid it all off.

95
07:07.907 --> 07:10.243
I don't have any debt left, so don't worry about it, please.

96
07:10.326 --> 07:11.410
For goodness' sake.

97
07:14.121 --> 07:15.331
That damn debt.

98
07:15.998 --> 07:18.709
I spent, I guess, pretty much my whole life on edge

99
07:19.293 --> 07:21.295
because of the choices your father made.

100
07:21.379 --> 07:24.131
Oh no. Come on, Mom. Are you drunk?

101
07:24.632 --> 07:27.969
Why do you always talk about someone who's not even here when you drink? Stop it.

102
07:28.052 --> 07:29.554
That's not what I was saying.

103
07:33.140 --> 07:34.308
It's because of money

104
07:35.268 --> 07:37.186
that your father ended up like that.

105
07:38.980 --> 07:40.815
And I just feel bad for him.

106
07:43.985 --> 07:46.279
CONSTRUCTION SITE, 18:00 - 02:00, NIGHT SHIFT 200X, THE LAST

107
07:46.362 --> 07:49.073
I think my dad worked a temp job at a construction site.

108
07:51.367 --> 07:52.868
So I went to one too.

109
07:54.078 --> 07:55.871
And that's where I heard about a door.

110
07:58.249 --> 08:00.418
What do you want to do now that you know about it?

111
08:00.501 --> 08:01.460
Uh…

112
08:03.170 --> 08:04.589
I want to find my dad.

113
08:06.757 --> 08:08.843
If he's even alive anymore, that is.

114
08:10.886 --> 08:13.389
I guess there's probably no hope, right?

115
08:13.472 --> 08:15.224
It's been 20 years already.

116
08:16.309 --> 08:17.310
Mm.

117
08:18.311 --> 08:22.023
Well, it's not exactly impossible, you know.

118
08:22.106 --> 08:24.942
If he crossed over to the other world, but didn't die in the process.

119
08:26.611 --> 08:28.112
Just like you already heard,

120
08:28.946 --> 08:30.781
the places where people work these jobs

121
08:32.074 --> 08:34.619
have a door that acts as a portal.

122
08:36.370 --> 08:37.580
And vice versa.

123
08:38.080 --> 08:40.916
There is a door that leads back to this world too.

124
08:42.209 --> 08:44.128
Wh… What do you mean, "a door?"

125
08:44.712 --> 08:46.922
There's an amusement park I wanna show you.

126
08:47.632 --> 08:49.383
The door I know about is there.

127
08:53.512 --> 08:55.097
But how…

128
08:55.681 --> 08:57.016
How do you know about it?

129
08:58.559 --> 09:00.770
Because I came back myself through that door.

130
09:01.270 --> 09:02.563
From the other world.

131
09:06.192 --> 09:08.152
WORKER'S RIGHTS

132
09:08.235 --> 09:10.488
…flutter over the wall! The warm…

133
09:10.571 --> 09:12.365
That was 40 years ago.

134
09:12.448 --> 09:14.325
Nice singing, ladies. Spray 'em all!

135
09:23.334 --> 09:26.629
At first, I thought that I could change the entire world.

136
09:29.256 --> 09:31.133
Hey, drag 'em out! All of them. Let's go!

137
09:36.514 --> 09:37.515
Catch her!

138
09:40.142 --> 09:41.477
Bitch!

139
09:41.560 --> 09:43.187
Drag them all out of here. Now!

140
09:43.270 --> 09:46.065
Bring that bitch over here!

141
09:47.066 --> 09:49.068
Come on. Right now. Come! Let's go!

142
09:50.569 --> 09:53.239
Hurry! Come on!

143
09:55.491 --> 09:56.492
Get in here.

144
09:58.411 --> 09:59.537
Drag them out!

145
09:59.620 --> 10:02.415
- Hide here until it's over. - No, no, I can't. I…

146
10:02.915 --> 10:04.834
Yeon-joo, you were here.

147
10:04.917 --> 10:08.129
You have to go out and tell the world. It's the only way we can change things.

148
10:11.298 --> 10:12.842
Get them all! Go!

149
10:13.801 --> 10:15.553
You're dead. You got that? Huh?

150
10:15.636 --> 10:17.638
- You hear what I said? - Over here right now!

151
10:19.724 --> 10:21.934
Come here, you stupid girl!

152
10:24.228 --> 10:26.272
Let go! Get off me! No!

153
10:32.570 --> 10:34.989
And I don't know how much time passed…

154
10:40.661 --> 10:43.247
but when the door opened, I looked around…

155
11:08.147 --> 11:10.733
…and saw that I was standing in an amusement park

156
11:11.233 --> 11:13.444
where the textile factory used to be.

157
11:24.622 --> 11:28.125
FANTASY HAUNTED HOUSE

158
11:28.209 --> 11:29.668
That was so crazy!

159
11:29.752 --> 11:32.838
No one remembered me. Not a single person around me.

160
11:38.052 --> 11:40.095
And that turned out to be a scary thing.

161
11:45.267 --> 11:48.813
It's very possible that your father wants to be found by someone.

162
11:49.313 --> 11:50.815
He's just somewhere waiting.

163
11:53.067 --> 11:56.237
I'll help you so that you have the best possible chance of finding him.

164
12:10.000 --> 12:12.628
Hey! Look who's here.

165
12:14.588 --> 12:16.674
Mr. Hyeok-jun finally came back.

166
12:17.800 --> 12:19.593
I've been waiting for so long.

167
12:20.511 --> 12:21.428
Come in.

168
12:23.264 --> 12:26.475
Let's see what we have. The jobs offered today are…

169
12:28.727 --> 12:29.728
Byeon Min-su.

170
12:32.398 --> 12:33.941
He did the jobs in there.

171
12:36.360 --> 12:37.778
You know about this guy?

172
12:38.904 --> 12:41.115
That's why I got sent to the construction site, right?

173
12:44.285 --> 12:46.161
It's just like I mentioned before,

174
12:46.954 --> 12:47.955
I don't know him.

175
12:48.038 --> 12:49.206
Isn't it that you do know him…

176
12:51.959 --> 12:53.460
but you can't tell me about it?

177
12:56.130 --> 12:57.548
You don't have to answer that.

178
12:59.091 --> 13:01.343
Just give me the temp job at the amusement park.

179
13:04.138 --> 13:05.431
The amusement park?

180
13:06.640 --> 13:08.225
How did you know about that?

181
13:27.661 --> 13:29.872
You okay with this? There are barely successful results.

182
13:29.955 --> 13:31.332
KYUNGIL NEO WORLD, PARADE PART-TIME

183
13:31.415 --> 13:33.459
FULL-TIME POSITION TRANSITION PROGRAM 10 P.M. - 4 A.M.

184
13:33.542 --> 13:35.419
It's a temp job that can become full-time.

185
13:36.754 --> 13:39.715
A full-time temp job? I don't understand.

186
13:39.798 --> 13:42.009
If you become a full-time employee,

187
13:43.928 --> 13:45.888
you could finally know about

188
13:47.014 --> 13:48.349
what you've been searching for.

189
14:06.575 --> 14:09.995
ACCEPT

190
14:11.538 --> 14:12.831
Just get through…

191
14:14.708 --> 14:16.043
Just get through the night.

192
14:19.421 --> 14:22.174
BYEON JI-YOON THINK I DID WELL AT THE INTERVIEW TODAY

193
14:22.257 --> 14:27.638
WILL COME OVER AFTER MEETING A FRIEND WANT ME TO BRING SOME FRIED CHICKEN?

194
14:40.693 --> 14:45.739
IF ANYTHING HAPPENS, TELL MOM…

195
14:53.831 --> 14:56.959
YOU DID WELL AT THE INTERVIEW, SO LET'S HAVE SOME FRIED CHICKEN

196
14:57.042 --> 15:04.049
I HAVE PLANS TOO, SO I'LL BE HOME LATE SEE YOU TONIGHT

197
15:05.676 --> 15:08.679
WELCOME TO THE JOY-FILLED NEO WORLD!

198
15:30.409 --> 15:31.535
This is the door.

199
15:34.663 --> 15:36.707
That? It's this one right here?

200
15:37.291 --> 15:39.752
This is… the portal door?

201
15:40.794 --> 15:41.670
Yes.

202
15:42.337 --> 15:43.839
The door I came out of.

203
15:52.306 --> 15:55.059
Looks like it's just a storage room.

204
15:57.311 --> 16:00.064
It'll be different when you're working the temp job at night.

205
16:07.196 --> 16:10.324
Be prepared. It won't be easy for you to get to the door.

206
16:10.824 --> 16:14.036
So just act natural as you work and wait for the right moment.

207
16:20.292 --> 16:22.419
It really does look nicer during the day.

208
16:39.895 --> 16:41.438
Oh! Uh…

209
16:41.522 --> 16:42.773
What the hell?

210
16:46.527 --> 16:48.112
Wh… Wh… What is this?

211
16:53.033 --> 16:54.535
Is anyone here?

212
16:58.330 --> 17:01.667
Excuse me? Hello? Anybody? I'm here for the temp job.

213
17:04.294 --> 17:05.629
Oh shit!

214
17:17.683 --> 17:19.351
Are you an employee here?

215
17:20.686 --> 17:22.980
Um… I'm here for the--

216
17:25.816 --> 17:27.234
Please come this way!

217
17:28.318 --> 17:30.112
All the others are already here.

218
17:32.406 --> 17:34.241
So? Shall we go?

219
17:36.994 --> 17:39.163
One, two, three, four…

220
17:44.626 --> 17:45.919
Let's get going now.

221
17:50.299 --> 17:54.553
One, two, three, four. One, two, three, four.

222
17:54.636 --> 17:56.763
One, two, three, four.

223
17:56.847 --> 18:00.267
One, two, three, four. One, two…

224
18:00.350 --> 18:02.352
KYUNGIL NEO WORLD PARADE PART-TIME JOB

225
18:02.436 --> 18:05.606
FULL-TIME POSITION TRANSITION PROGRAM STARTS AT 10 P.M., ENDS AT 4 A.M

226
18:08.775 --> 18:11.195
Two, two, three four.

227
18:11.695 --> 18:16.450
One, two, three, four. Two, two, three, four.

228
18:16.533 --> 18:18.285
One, two… Stop!

229
18:22.122 --> 18:22.956
The head.

230
18:23.457 --> 18:24.833
Get it on now.

231
18:27.628 --> 18:29.171
Oh, uh, yeah.

232
18:35.802 --> 18:37.012
All right.

233
18:37.554 --> 18:38.847
Now that we're ready,

234
18:38.931 --> 18:40.974
I bet you can guess what fable we're in.

235
18:42.059 --> 18:45.062
That's right! "The Three Little Pigs" is the story.

236
18:49.691 --> 18:50.734
Okay, Wolf.

237
18:50.817 --> 18:52.277
The pigs are here.

238
18:53.111 --> 18:54.655
Boy, what can he do?

239
18:56.031 --> 18:59.493
Oh, uh, chase after the pigs, or something like that?

240
19:03.580 --> 19:05.415
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!

241
19:05.958 --> 19:07.626
That's right!

242
19:07.709 --> 19:10.045
That's the thing the wolf should do.

243
19:11.797 --> 19:13.966
The wolf shouldn't speak like a human, should he?

244
19:19.054 --> 19:20.847
- Shall we jump right into it? - Uh…

245
19:24.476 --> 19:25.435
Music.

246
19:26.270 --> 19:27.104
Cue!

247
19:30.148 --> 19:31.358
Oh God. Uh…

248
19:31.441 --> 19:34.236
The wolf should feel free to improvise!

249
19:36.113 --> 19:38.865
Come on! You have to catch them! Try again!

250
19:41.368 --> 19:42.411
Hey, stop!

251
19:45.831 --> 19:48.917
Come on, catch the pigs! Go catch them!

252
19:51.044 --> 19:52.170
Agh!

253
19:55.799 --> 19:57.843
What did those guys do before this gig?

254
20:00.053 --> 20:03.015
Okay! Let's switch it up, shall we?

255
20:03.098 --> 20:05.017
Music. Cue!

256
20:07.811 --> 20:08.895
Oh God. What now?

257
20:23.201 --> 20:24.494
- Pigs. - What the hell?

258
20:24.578 --> 20:25.746
It's your turn now.

259
20:28.290 --> 20:30.667
Oh. Oh!

260
20:30.751 --> 20:33.086
Hyeok-jun, I brought fried chicken. Get out here.

261
20:35.589 --> 20:36.631
Oh, right.

262
20:37.632 --> 20:38.925
He's busy tonight.

263
20:55.609 --> 20:56.568
Wait, what?

264
20:57.527 --> 20:59.237
Why is it so clean in here?

265
21:36.400 --> 21:39.277
CONVENIENCE STORE, MANAGER, MILK DELIVERY CLINICAL TRIAL, CONSTRUCTION SITE

266
21:39.361 --> 21:43.490
THE LAST PART-TIME JOB FIND DAD

267
21:43.573 --> 21:44.866
"Find Dad"?

268
21:45.575 --> 21:47.953
Agh, no! H… Hold on! Whoa, whoa. Get away!

269
21:50.872 --> 21:53.375
Hey, stop, wait! You said I'm the villain. I'm the wolf!

270
21:53.458 --> 21:56.420
Forget the old fable about only the three little pigs getting chased.

271
21:56.503 --> 21:58.255
In here, they get to hunt too!

272
21:58.338 --> 21:59.381
Ah, shi…

273
22:00.090 --> 22:01.967
- Oh! Oh. - Oh!

274
22:16.022 --> 22:16.982
Enough!

275
22:18.150 --> 22:19.568
That's it.

276
22:19.651 --> 22:21.528
Stop there.

277
22:22.988 --> 22:25.407
Oh! You got the wolf!

278
22:25.490 --> 22:28.952
What a great job you did, my little piggies. Rehearsal can stop now.

279
22:34.666 --> 22:36.042
This is batshit crazy.

280
22:38.795 --> 22:41.256
On the stage, image is everything. The mask always must stay on.

281
22:41.339 --> 22:43.925
You'll become a target for everybody if you try removing the mask.

282
22:45.302 --> 22:46.595
Put more heart into it.

283
22:46.678 --> 22:49.723
During the real thing, we're going to need greater commitment.

284
22:49.806 --> 22:51.433
Uh, yeah, yeah, I get it.

285
22:51.516 --> 22:53.643
And don't use human language.

286
22:54.478 --> 22:57.147
Okay, shall we go on to the parade?

287
22:58.106 --> 23:00.442
Right, left, right, left.

288
23:00.525 --> 23:02.819
Chassé right, chassé left.

289
23:02.903 --> 23:07.365
Right, left, right, left. Look excited, everyone, and off we go!

290
23:07.449 --> 23:09.993
Right, left, right, left.

291
23:10.076 --> 23:12.454
Chassé right, chassé left.

292
23:16.583 --> 23:18.460
Music… Change!

293
23:18.543 --> 23:20.545
What? Already?

294
23:20.629 --> 23:22.714
Donkey with the first hit!

295
23:29.429 --> 23:31.264
Wolf! What are you doing? Just spacing out?

296
23:31.348 --> 23:32.933
Look! The pigs are all getting away!

297
23:33.892 --> 23:36.895
Reverse. Music. Go!

298
23:36.978 --> 23:38.230
Oh, no, what do I do?

299
23:39.189 --> 23:40.190
Reverse?

300
23:40.273 --> 23:44.611
Wolf, you better run away quickly! All right, pigs, go, go, go!

301
23:44.694 --> 23:46.571
Get him! Let's get moving!

302
23:54.746 --> 23:58.166
Hey, wolf! Where are you going? You have to move along the parade route!

303
23:58.250 --> 23:59.251
Seriously?

304
24:14.391 --> 24:16.434
I told you not to give my brother any more jobs!

305
24:16.518 --> 24:18.895
That kid almost died and you sent him back again?

306
24:18.979 --> 24:21.565
You and those monsters are on the same side. You're a fucking devil!

307
24:21.648 --> 24:24.109
Why don't you just die? I'll kill you, I swear!

308
24:30.115 --> 24:31.408
We have faith in common.

309
24:31.908 --> 24:34.619
Huh?

310
24:40.500 --> 24:41.459
Ms. Ji-yoon,

311
24:42.586 --> 24:45.171
take a deep breath, and let me talk for a minute.

312
24:47.674 --> 24:50.343
There was someone who kept appearing to you and your brother, correct?

313
24:55.557 --> 24:56.433
This person.

314
24:58.059 --> 24:58.935
What?

315
24:59.728 --> 25:00.645
This is…

316
25:03.148 --> 25:06.776
This is that, uh… What was it? She's a workers' something--

317
25:06.860 --> 25:08.987
The Workers' Compensation Service accident investigator?

318
25:09.070 --> 25:09.988
That's right.

319
25:11.239 --> 25:14.409
That organization was disbanded in the 1980s.

320
25:14.909 --> 25:16.745
That woman's not human.

321
25:17.954 --> 25:18.830
What?

322
25:24.210 --> 25:26.421
She's a monster that came from the other side.

323
25:35.138 --> 25:36.890
Unfortunately for your brother,

324
25:36.973 --> 25:38.933
he's simply being used right now.

325
25:41.186 --> 25:45.482
She's so diligent the surveillance network didn't catch her.

326
25:45.565 --> 25:47.359
She's extremely intelligent.

327
25:48.902 --> 25:50.820
I've dealt with a lot of monsters.

328
25:50.904 --> 25:54.282
However, she is the only one with such a sense of self.

329
25:56.868 --> 25:57.869
All right.

330
25:58.870 --> 26:00.121
That monster?

331
26:00.789 --> 26:03.875
I will be the one who handles it. So you can go home now.

332
26:03.958 --> 26:06.127
And pray that your brother gets to finish his gig

333
26:06.211 --> 26:07.504
and get out safely.

334
26:16.805 --> 26:18.014
Ms. Ji-yoon!

335
26:45.417 --> 26:47.836
Ah, shi…

336
27:15.989 --> 27:16.865
Oh shit.

337
27:21.745 --> 27:24.247
Uh, hey, man… Uh, hey, do you…

338
27:24.330 --> 27:25.498
Oh! Uh…

339
27:25.999 --> 27:27.292
Oh my God.

340
27:28.418 --> 27:30.587
- Take it off for me. - What?

341
27:31.588 --> 27:34.799
Please get this off of me.

342
27:34.883 --> 27:36.801
I'll get it. Hold on.

343
27:54.068 --> 27:55.320
What… I… I'm sorry!

344
28:00.033 --> 28:01.367
N… No way.

345
28:26.100 --> 28:26.935
Shi…

346
28:31.815 --> 28:35.360
And now, shall we begin the grand finale?

347
28:39.197 --> 28:42.909
You guys are getting closer to becoming full-time employees.

348
28:45.495 --> 28:46.996
Shi…

349
28:52.210 --> 28:53.461
Give it a little more energy!

350
28:53.545 --> 28:57.549
Come on, you have to keep going until there's only one left.

351
28:58.049 --> 28:59.217
Yes! That's it!

352
29:02.720 --> 29:04.472
Hi there!

353
29:06.891 --> 29:08.101
Stop!

354
29:08.184 --> 29:11.396
A defective character without his costume has appeared.

355
29:14.065 --> 29:16.943
Let's clean it up now. Sanitation!

356
29:18.403 --> 29:20.238
Oh! Whoa! Oh.

357
29:21.114 --> 29:22.740
Agh! Oh!

358
29:24.617 --> 29:25.952
Hey, stay away!

359
29:28.788 --> 29:31.499
Agh!

360
29:39.424 --> 29:41.885
Hey!

361
29:51.311 --> 29:52.312
Oh!

362
30:06.910 --> 30:08.369
FANTASY HAUNTED HOUSE

363
30:08.453 --> 30:10.079
"FANTASY"

364
30:26.220 --> 30:27.263
Oh! Agh!

365
30:29.140 --> 30:30.391
Uh. Oh.

366
30:43.488 --> 30:46.991
Welcome! Challenge! A Father's Miracle is starting right now.

367
30:49.327 --> 30:52.455
Gather your loved ones for this heartwarming, thrilling show.

368
30:52.538 --> 30:55.875
The whole family can enjoy Challenge! A Father's Miracle together!

369
30:56.709 --> 30:59.253
The father has a mission he's received, so what will it be today?

370
30:59.337 --> 31:02.882
The miracle mission this father will perform today is this!

371
31:08.137 --> 31:09.347
This can't be real.
